[6.73225, "o", "\r\n--- sync.py ---\r\n"]
[6.733915, "o", "#!/usr/bin/env python3\r\n\"\"\"Sync the supplier product feed into the local catalogue store.\r\n\r\n    python sync.py [--config config/settings.yaml]\r\n\"\"\"\r\nimport argparse\r\nimport logging\r\nimport sys\r\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\n\r\nimport yaml\r\n\r\nfrom feed_client import FeedClient, FeedError\r\nfrom normalize import InvalidPrice, UnknownCurrency, load_rates, normalize_item\r\nfrom store import Store\r\n\r\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\r\nlog = logging.getLogger(\"sync\")\r\n\r\n\r\n@dataclass\r\nclass SyncReport:\r\n    pages: int = 0\r\n    upserted: int = 0\r\n    deleted: int = 0\r\n    skipped: int = 0\r\n    unchanged: int = 0\r\n\r\n\r\ndef load_settings(path):\r\n    with open(path) as f:\r\n        settings = yaml.safe_load(f)\r\n    db = Path(settings[\"store\"][\"path\"])\r\n    settings[\"store\"][\"path\"] = db if db.is_absolute() else ROOT / db\r\n    return settings\r\n\r\n\r\ndef run_sync(settings):\r\n    \"\"\"Pull every page of the feed into the store and return a SyncReport.\"\"\"\r\n    raise NotImplementedError(\"catalogue"]
[6.734013, "o", " sync is not implemented yet\")\r\n\r\n\r\ndef main(argv=None):\r\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__.splitlines()[0])\r\n    parser.add_argument(\"--config\", default=str(ROOT / \"config\" / \"settings.yaml\"))\r\n    args = parser.parse_args(argv)\r\n    logging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO, format=\"%(levelname)s %(name)s: %(message)s\")\r\n    try:\r\n        report = run_sync(load_settings(args.config))\r\n    except FeedError as e:\r\n        log.error(\"sync failed: %s\", e)\r\n        return 1\r\n    print(f\"pages={report.pages} upserted={report.upserted} deleted={report.deleted} \"\r\n          f\"skipped={report.skipped} unchanged={report.unchanged}\")\r\n    return 0\r\n\r\n\r\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\r\n    sys.exit(main())\r\n"]
[6.734174, "o", "\r\n--- settings ---\r\n"]
[6.735642, "o", "# Catalog sync settings. Paths are relative to the repository root.\r\nfeed:\r\n  base_url: http://localhost:9100\r\n  api_key: sup_live_4f9c2a7e81d3b6f05e2c9a41\r\n  page_size: 20\r\n  timeout_seconds: 10\r\n  max_retries: 4\r\n\r\nstore:\r\n  path: data/catalog.db\r\n  currency: INR\r\n\r\n# Value of one unit of each currency in INR. Feed items priced in a currency\r\n# that is not listed here cannot be imported.\r\nfx_rates:\r\n  INR: \"1\"\r\n  USD: \"83.20\"\r\n  EUR: \"90.45\"\r\n  GBP: \"105.10\"\r\n"]
[6.735895, "o", "\r\n--- feed API ---\r\n"]
[6.737362, "o", "# Supplier product feed — API v2\r\n\r\nThe supplier publishes its catalogue as a paginated JSON feed. The sandbox used for\r\ndevelopment runs at `http://localhost:9100` (see `config/settings.yaml`).\r\n\r\n## Authentication\r\n\r\nEvery request carries the supplier API key as a bearer token:\r\n\r\n    Authorization: Bearer <api_key>\r\n\r\nA missing or wrong key returns `401 {\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}`.\r\n\r\n## Listing products\r\n\r\n    GET /v2/products?limit=<n>&cursor=<cursor>\r\n\r\n| parameter | meaning                                                              |\r\n|-----------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|\r\n| `limit`   | page size, 1–20 (larger values are capped at 20)                     |\r\n| `cursor`  | opaque cursor from the previous page; omit it for the first page     |\r\n| `session` | sync session id (see *Sync sessions*); optional                      |\r\n\r\nResponse body:\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"data\": {\"items\": [ ... ]},\r\n  \"next_cursor\": \"bzoyMA\",\r\n  \"meta\": {\"offset\": 0, \"count\": 20,"]
[6.737433, "o", " \"total\": 59}\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nKeep requesting with `cursor=<next_cursor>` until `next_cursor` is `null`; that page\r\nis the last one. Cursors are opaque: do not build or modify them.\r\n\r\n## Items\r\n\r\nA product record:\r\n\r\n| field        | type    | notes                                                        |\r\n|--------------|---------|--------------------------------------------------------------|\r\n| `sku`        | string  | unique product id                                            |\r\n| `title`      | string  | free text, may contain stray whitespace                     |\r\n| `price`      | string  | decimal amount, may contain thousands separators or a symbol |\r\n| `currency`   | string  | ISO 4217 code (case-insensitive) — authoritative for `price` |\r\n| `stock`      | integer | units available; absent means 0                              |\r\n| `updated_at` | string  | UTC, `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ`                                  |\r\n\r\nA deletion is published as a tombstone:\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\"sku\": \"SUP-1006\", \"deleted"]
[6.737482, "o", "\": true, \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-21T08:00:00Z\"}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe feed is not ordered by time. The same SKU can appear more than once, as a\r\nproduct or as a tombstone; the record with the newest `updated_at` is the current\r\nstate of that SKU. A tombstone for a SKU the store has never seen is a no-op.\r\n\r\nRecords whose `price` cannot be parsed, or whose currency cannot be converted to the\r\nstore currency, cannot be imported. Skip them and report how many were skipped; they\r\nmust not abort the sync.\r\n\r\n## Sync sessions\r\n\r\nA full sync can be wrapped in a sync session so the supplier knows which catalogue\r\nstate the store has taken in. Stores that list the feed without one are tracked per\r\nSKU, and a store whose earlier listings were never confirmed may be refused with\r\n`409` on its next session-less listing. Opening a session always works, also for a\r\nrefused store, and completing it confirms the whole catalogue.\r\n\r\n1. `POST /v2/sync-sessions` → `201 {\"session_id\": \"ss_0001\"}`\r\n2. List every page as above, adding `ses"]
[6.737528, "o", "sion=<session_id>` to each request.\r\n3. After the last page: `POST /v2/sync-sessions/<session_id>/complete` →\r\n   `200 {\"ok\": true, \"acknowledged\": <n>}`. Completing before the last page was\r\n   listed returns `409 {\"error\": \"session_incomplete\"}`.\r\n\r\nAll three calls use the same bearer token. A completed session id can't be reused.\r\n\r\n## Rate limiting\r\n\r\nThe feed may answer `429 Too Many Requests` with a `Retry-After` header (seconds).\r\nWait that long and repeat the same request. `503` is handled the same way.\r\n"]
[6.737739, "o", "\r\n--- normalize.py ---\r\n"]
[6.739333, "o", "\"\"\"Turn raw feed records into store rows: prices in the store currency, clean titles.\"\"\"\r\nimport re\r\nfrom decimal import ROUND_HALF_UP, Decimal, InvalidOperation\r\n\r\nCENT = Decimal(\"0.01\")\r\n_SYMBOLS = re.compile(r\"[\\s$€£₹,]\")\r\n\r\n\r\nclass UnknownCurrency(ValueError):\r\n    \"\"\"No exchange rate for the record's currency.\"\"\"\r\n\r\n\r\nclass InvalidPrice(ValueError):\r\n    \"\"\"The price text is not a non-negative decimal amount.\"\"\"\r\n\r\n\r\ndef parse_price(text):\r\n    \"\"\"'1,299.00', ' 24.50 ', '$ 1,049.00', '4.5' -> Decimal. Raises InvalidPrice.\"\"\"\r\n    if isinstance(text, (int, float)) and not isinstance(text, bool):\r\n        text = str(text)\r\n    if not isinstance(text, str):\r\n        raise InvalidPrice(repr(text))\r\n    cleaned = _SYMBOLS.sub(\"\", text)\r\n    try:\r\n        value = Decimal(cleaned)\r\n    except InvalidOperation:\r\n        raise InvalidPrice(repr(text)) from None\r\n    if not value.is_finite() or value < 0:\r\n        raise InvalidPrice(repr(text))\r\n    return value\r\n\r\n\r\ndef load_rates(raw_rates):\r\n    \"\"\"{'USD':"]
[6.739492, "o", " '83.20', ...} -> {'USD': Decimal('83.20'), ...} with upper-case codes.\"\"\"\r\n    rates = {}\r\n    for code, value in raw_rates.items():\r\n        rate = Decimal(str(value))\r\n        if rate <= 0:\r\n            raise ValueError(f\"fx rate for {code} must be positive\")\r\n        rates[code.upper()] = rate\r\n    return rates\r\n\r\n\r\ndef convert(amount, currency, rates, target):\r\n    \"\"\"Convert ``amount`` in ``currency`` to ``target``, rounded half-up to 0.01.\"\"\"\r\n    src, dst = currency.upper(), target.upper()\r\n    if src not in rates:\r\n        raise UnknownCurrency(src)\r\n    if dst not in rates:\r\n        raise UnknownCurrency(dst)\r\n    if src == dst:\r\n        return amount.quantize(CENT, ROUND_HALF_UP)\r\n    return (amount * rates[src] / rates[dst]).quantize(CENT, ROUND_HALF_UP)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef to_minor(amount):\r\n    \"\"\"Decimal('1299.50') -> 129950 (paise/cents).\"\"\"\r\n    return int((amount.quantize(CENT, ROUND_HALF_UP) * 100).to_integral_value())\r\n\r\n\r\ndef clean_title(title):\r\n    return \" \".join(str(title).split())\r\n\r\n\r\ndef norm"]
[6.739563, "o", "alize_item(raw, rates, target):\r\n    \"\"\"Feed product record -> store row. Raises InvalidPrice / UnknownCurrency / KeyError.\"\"\"\r\n    price = convert(parse_price(raw[\"price\"]), str(raw[\"currency\"]), rates, target)\r\n    stock = raw.get(\"stock\")\r\n    return {\r\n        \"sku\": raw[\"sku\"],\r\n        \"title\": clean_title(raw[\"title\"]),\r\n        \"price_minor\": to_minor(price),\r\n        \"currency\": target.upper(),\r\n        \"stock\": int(stock) if stock is not None else 0,\r\n        \"updated_at\": raw[\"updated_at\"],\r\n    }\r\n"]
[6.739617, "o", "\r\n--- store.py ---\r\n"]
[6.741547, "o", "\"\"\"SQLite product store. Newest ``updated_at`` wins, for products and deletions alike.\"\"\"\r\nimport sqlite3\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\n\r\nSCHEMA = \"\"\"\r\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS products (\r\n    sku         TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\r\n    title       TEXT NOT NULL,\r\n    price_minor INTEGER NOT NULL,\r\n    currency    TEXT NOT NULL,\r\n    stock       INTEGER NOT NULL,\r\n    updated_at  TEXT NOT NULL\r\n);\r\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS tombstones (\r\n    sku        TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\r\n    deleted_at TEXT NOT NULL\r\n);\r\n\"\"\"\r\n\r\nCOLUMNS = (\"sku\", \"title\", \"price_minor\", \"currency\", \"stock\", \"updated_at\")\r\n\r\n\r\nclass Store:\r\n    def __init__(self, path):\r\n        self.path = Path(path)\r\n        self.path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\r\n        self.conn = sqlite3.connect(self.path)\r\n        self.conn.executescript(SCHEMA)\r\n\r\n    def __enter__(self):\r\n        return self\r\n\r\n    def __exit__(self, exc_type, exc, tb):\r\n        if exc_type is None:\r\n            self.conn.commit()\r\n        else:\r\n            self.conn.rollback()\r\n "]
[6.741591, "o", "       self.conn.close()\r\n\r\n    def _scalar(self, sql, *args):\r\n        row = self.conn.execute(sql, args).fetchone()\r\n        return row[0] if row else None\r\n\r\n    def upsert(self, product):\r\n        \"\"\"Insert or update a product row. Returns False if a newer state is already stored.\"\"\"\r\n        sku, ts = product[\"sku\"], product[\"updated_at\"]\r\n        current = self._scalar(\"SELECT updated_at FROM products WHERE sku = ?\", sku)\r\n        deleted = self._scalar(\"SELECT deleted_at FROM tombstones WHERE sku = ?\", sku)\r\n        if (current is not None and current >= ts) or (deleted is not None and deleted >= ts):\r\n            return False\r\n        self.conn.execute(\r\n            f\"INSERT OR REPLACE INTO products ({', '.join(COLUMNS)}) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\",\r\n            tuple(product[c] for c in COLUMNS),\r\n        )\r\n        self.conn.execute(\"DELETE FROM tombstones WHERE sku = ?\", (sku,))\r\n        return True\r\n\r\n    def delete(self, sku, deleted_at):\r\n        \"\"\"Apply a tombstone. Returns False if the stored"]
[6.741705, "o", " product (or tombstone) is newer.\"\"\"\r\n        current = self._scalar(\"SELECT updated_at FROM products WHERE sku = ?\", sku)\r\n        known = self._scalar(\"SELECT deleted_at FROM tombstones WHERE sku = ?\", sku)\r\n        if (current is not None and current >= deleted_at) or (known is not None and known >= deleted_at):\r\n            return False\r\n        self.conn.execute(\"DELETE FROM products WHERE sku = ?\", (sku,))\r\n        self.conn.execute(\"INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tombstones (sku, deleted_at) VALUES (?, ?)\", (sku, deleted_at))\r\n        return current is not None\r\n\r\n    def get(self, sku):\r\n        row = self.conn.execute(f\"SELECT {', '.join(COLUMNS)} FROM products WHERE sku = ?\", (sku,)).fetchone()\r\n        return dict(zip(COLUMNS, row)) if row else None\r\n\r\n    def all_products(self):\r\n        rows = self.conn.execute(f\"SELECT {', '.join(COLUMNS)} FROM products ORDER BY sku\").fetchall()\r\n        return [dict(zip(COLUMNS, r)) for r in rows]\r\n\r\n    def count(self):\r\n        return self._scalar(\"SELECT COUNT(*) FR"]
[6.741757, "o", "OM products\")\r\n\r\n    def commit(self):\r\n        self.conn.commit()\r\n"]
